WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:01.980
<b>Unagi</b>

00:00.120 --> 00:01.980
<b>Unagi</b>

00:01.980 --> 00:03.980
<b>Unagi</b>

00:01.980 --> 00:03.980
Say, Jujoji.

00:03.980 --> 00:08.760
Have you ever been to an authentic 
unagi shop like this by yourself?

00:08.760 --> 00:11.140
No, I can't say that I have.

00:11.820 --> 00:13.860
The unagi is definitely 
good, but the price...

00:13.860 --> 00:16.740
<b>Menu
 Unaju Regular 3,000 yen
 Special 4,500 yen
 Extra Special 6,700 yen</b>

00:14.110 --> 00:16.740
Not to mention, just setting 
foot in a place like this

00:16.740 --> 00:20.620
tends to demand a certain age
or level of experience.

00:20.620 --> 00:22.500
Yeah...

00:22.780 --> 00:24.620
So what's going on over there?

00:25.260 --> 00:26.880
I couldn't say...

00:30.940 --> 00:33.010
The extra special unaju, please!

02:03.320 --> 02:05.360
How old does she look to you?

02:05.360 --> 02:08.480
A high school girl? 
No, maybe middle school...

02:08.720 --> 02:11.460
Though her appearance and 
behavior seem mature.

02:11.460 --> 02:15.500
So she's probably a sheltered rich girl.

02:22.090 --> 02:24.150
Kajio, stop staring.

02:24.150 --> 02:25.310
What a mystery.

02:25.310 --> 02:29.510
A young girl alone at an unagi shop, 
ordering the extra special unaju...

02:29.960 --> 02:32.900
She looks like a doll. Does she 
even have any internal organs?

02:32.900 --> 02:35.170
She couldn't eat unagi if 
she didn't have organs.

02:35.420 --> 02:38.240
Maybe she's a puppet that eats unaju.

02:38.240 --> 02:41.490
Specifically unaju? You seem 
really worried about this.

02:41.490 --> 02:42.930
You're that concerned?

02:42.930 --> 02:44.930
Mysteries shouldn't exist...

02:44.930 --> 02:49.110
To ensure that your food tastes better 
and that you can sleep soundly at night.

02:49.720 --> 02:53.180
Today's the last day I want 
something like that in my life.

02:54.420 --> 02:57.290
Let's forget about why she 
might be here for the moment.

02:57.290 --> 03:01.590
Why did you invite me out of the blue 
to eat unagi for lunch with you?

03:01.890 --> 03:03.870
And at such a fancy place, no less?

03:05.080 --> 03:08.580
It's been six months since 
my wife Yukie passed.

03:09.220 --> 03:12.390
Ever since Yukie passed, 
my body just feels so heavy,

03:12.390 --> 03:14.590
and I go for days without getting any sleep.

03:14.900 --> 03:18.640
I went to the hospital, but they 
can't find anything wrong with me.

03:18.640 --> 03:22.220
In the end, it's a psychogenic health problem.

03:22.570 --> 03:26.630
I guess it's hard to just 
set your heart free.

03:28.140 --> 03:30.600
But now, things seem back to normal.

03:30.900 --> 03:34.480
I've been able to sleep these past few days, 
and I'm gaining some weight back.

03:34.480 --> 03:37.370
I figured it's time to get back on my feet.

03:37.370 --> 03:41.230
To celebrate, I thought I'd eat some unagi.

03:41.550 --> 03:46.370
I see. Well, your wife's passing 
did seem to do a number on you...

03:46.730 --> 03:49.490
Then you should indeed eat some unagi.

03:49.490 --> 03:52.310
It's been known to be good for 
you ever since the Nara period.

03:52.790 --> 03:55.580
According to the Manyoshu, 
it's good for heatstroke, as well.

03:55.580 --> 03:56.840
Wow...

03:56.840 --> 04:01.070
You always know the most useless trivia.

04:01.070 --> 04:04.550
Kimoyaki and umaki... Let's throw 
in some hone senbei, as well.

04:04.550 --> 04:06.210
Ma'am, we'd like to order.

04:06.210 --> 04:07.720
Sure, be right there.

04:08.070 --> 04:09.600
Let's look at this differently.

04:09.600 --> 04:10.680
Hm?

04:10.680 --> 04:15.930
It's hard to deduce why this girl is 
here with the information at hand.

04:15.930 --> 04:16.980
Well, yeah.

04:16.980 --> 04:19.000
Let's think about this instead.

04:19.350 --> 04:22.990
How did we end up encountering 
such a bizarre sight?

04:23.300 --> 04:27.160
Whenever something rare 
or strange happens to you,

04:27.160 --> 04:30.490
it's always been considered either 
a good omen or a bad omen.

04:30.490 --> 04:34.200
Perhaps this is some kind of sign for us.

04:34.200 --> 04:35.000
A sign?

04:35.310 --> 04:40.000
Like how they say something bad will 
happen if a black cat crosses your path,

04:40.000 --> 04:42.590
or something good will happen if 
a tea stalk is upright in your tea.

04:43.470 --> 04:46.590
I guess they do say that running 
into a hearse is bad luck.

04:46.590 --> 04:52.460
So what does seeing a girl eating unaju by 
herself at an authentic unagi shop mean?

04:53.070 --> 04:57.500
Considering how elegant she looks, 
I'd like to see it as a good omen...

04:58.130 --> 04:59.860
The fact that such an eye-catching beauty,

05:00.170 --> 05:05.580
who may or may not even be human, 
appeared in a place like this

05:05.580 --> 05:08.030
must have some meaning 
or symbolism behind it.

05:08.030 --> 05:08.870
Mhm.

05:09.550 --> 05:11.150
Unagi are considered messengers

05:11.540 --> 05:14.620
for deities, particularly for Kokuzo Bosatsu.

05:15.390 --> 05:19.130
Kokuzo Bosatsu is known as the 
god of fortune and wisdom.

05:19.130 --> 05:22.290
In his left hand, he holds Chintamani 
stones that symbolizes fortune,

05:22.290 --> 05:25.050
and in his right hand, a treasured 
sword that symbolizes wisdom.

05:25.050 --> 05:26.890
Huh... Wisdom, eh?

05:26.890 --> 05:28.410
Another thing about unagi is that

05:28.410 --> 05:30.970
they're cut differently in Kansai 
than they are in Kanto.

05:31.390 --> 05:33.340
In the Kanto region, 
they cut down the back,

05:33.340 --> 05:35.480
and in Kansai, they cut down the belly.

05:35.810 --> 05:37.240
There were many samurai in Kanto,

05:37.240 --> 05:39.990
so they apparently wanted to avoid 
making it look like seppuku.

05:39.990 --> 05:41.730
That is one theory...

05:41.730 --> 05:45.740
But it's also said that they simply prepare 
it differently in the east and the west.

05:46.100 --> 05:47.700
It looks like this particular shop...

05:49.150 --> 05:51.660
prepares unagi in the Kansai way.

05:52.210 --> 05:55.680
Which means they open up the belly 
like someone committing seppuku.

05:55.680 --> 05:58.650
And because unagi are so hard to grasp,

05:58.650 --> 06:01.310
they're used in metaphors 
about skillfully running away.

06:01.990 --> 06:03.670
Putting all of these things together,

06:03.670 --> 06:06.920
that otherworldly girl 
represents the Kokuzo Bosatsu,

06:06.920 --> 06:11.050
and the unagi represents a criminal 
trying to run away from their crime.

06:11.380 --> 06:15.080
So the Kokuzo Bosatsu is capturing 
the criminal running from their crime

06:15.080 --> 06:16.810
with his treasured sword of wisdom,

06:16.810 --> 06:19.190
and trying to force them into seppuku.

06:19.190 --> 06:21.510
Man, that all came together nicely.

06:21.510 --> 06:22.190
Yes.

06:22.580 --> 06:26.730
That girl appearing here may 
be a revelation by someone wise

06:26.730 --> 06:29.450
who will reveal the sinner and 
punish them for their crimes.

06:30.110 --> 06:31.700
Kajio, you...

06:32.490 --> 06:33.700
You...

06:35.160 --> 06:36.710
killed your wife, Yukie-san, didn't you?

06:40.710 --> 06:42.540
You know, I've been thinking.

06:42.540 --> 06:44.810
Is it really okay for 
Kokuzo Bosatsu to eat unagi,

06:44.810 --> 06:47.320
considering they're supposed 
to be his messengers?

06:47.800 --> 06:48.970
I'm sure Bosatsu is able to

06:48.970 --> 06:52.170
freely determine how he wants 
to handle his messengers.

06:52.930 --> 06:56.430
All right... Why do you think I killed Yukie?

06:56.430 --> 07:00.850
Six months ago, Yukie was 
attacked by a mugger at night.

07:00.850 --> 07:03.570
They took her bag and
knocked her over, and she fell.

07:03.570 --> 07:07.230
She hit her head hard and, 
unfortunately, died as a result.

07:07.640 --> 07:11.170
That's just what was deduced 
based on how the body was found.

07:11.580 --> 07:15.240
No one witnessed the moment 
she was attacked by the mugger.

07:16.230 --> 07:19.260
After you hit Yukie-san and killed her,

07:19.260 --> 07:22.750
you could have easily made it look 
like she was attacked by a mugger.

07:24.000 --> 07:26.060
Though it wasn't murder,

07:26.060 --> 07:30.510
there have been similar incidents that 
occurred before Yukie was attacked.

07:30.760 --> 07:33.460
There have been several incidents 
since Yukie's death, as well.

07:33.460 --> 07:36.850
That's why they were investigating 
her death as a mugging.

07:37.140 --> 07:40.810
But if you had killed Yukie-san 
to make it look like a mugging,

07:40.810 --> 07:42.180
nothing would seem suspicious.

07:42.510 --> 07:47.330
Or it could even be said that perhaps 
you had committed the string of muggings

07:47.330 --> 07:50.110
so that you could hide your true motive.

07:50.570 --> 07:52.320
They still haven't caught the mugger.

07:52.320 --> 07:55.220
<b>Beware of Muggers!</b>

07:52.750 --> 07:55.360
As long as no one other than 
Yukie-san was found dead,

07:53.570 --> 07:58.580
<b>If you spot one, call 110!</b>

07:55.360 --> 07:58.580
it's not that risky a crime 
for the sake of camouflage.

07:58.930 --> 08:02.540
Yukie-san got sick of how clingy 
and controlling you had become,

08:02.540 --> 08:04.460
and wanted to divorce you.

08:05.030 --> 08:06.360
But knowing how you are,

08:06.360 --> 08:10.360
there's no way you'd ever let 
Yukie-san end up with another man.

08:10.950 --> 08:13.560
Actually, it's entirely believable 
that you'd kill her

08:13.560 --> 08:16.350
just so you could keep her yours forever.

08:16.350 --> 08:17.850
Where's your proof?

08:19.600 --> 08:21.480
I have no physical proof.

08:21.740 --> 08:27.480
But the fact that you couldn't sleep 
and lost weight after Yukie-san's death

08:27.480 --> 08:29.960
is all the proof I need.

08:29.960 --> 08:31.990
And what do you mean by that?

08:32.760 --> 08:36.990
You're not the type to mope around 
just because Yukie-san was killed.

08:37.370 --> 08:40.560
You would fly into a burning rage 
and do everything you could to find

08:40.560 --> 08:42.120
the mugger who killed your wife,

08:42.340 --> 08:44.370
and concentrate solely on getting revenge.

08:44.370 --> 08:46.670
Yukie-san belonged to you.

08:46.670 --> 08:50.750
There's no way you'd let anyone get 
away with doing anything to her.

08:51.160 --> 08:52.380
For the sake of argument,

08:52.380 --> 08:54.510
now that Yukie-san is dead,

08:54.510 --> 08:57.470
you don't have to worry about 
her belonging to any other man.

08:57.470 --> 09:01.640
You decide that works out in the end 
and let the mugger off the hook.

09:01.930 --> 09:05.690
That would mean you're 
satisfied with that outcome.

09:05.690 --> 09:07.950
You may not outwardly seem happy about it,

09:07.950 --> 09:10.270
but you'd be able to carry 
on as you did before.

09:10.620 --> 09:11.900
You'd never give in to anxiety

09:11.900 --> 09:14.970
or let yourself become whittled 
down mentally or physically.

09:15.500 --> 09:16.120
Mhm.

09:16.120 --> 09:17.490
<i>He's right about that.</i>

09:18.040 --> 09:21.980
But you were clearly worn down, 
like any normal husband would be

09:21.980 --> 09:23.450
after losing his beloved wife.

09:24.050 --> 09:26.210
Kajio, are you all right?

09:26.210 --> 09:29.710
Y-Yeah... Sorry. I just got dizzy.

09:30.350 --> 09:31.580
Inconceivable.

09:31.580 --> 09:33.710
That must've been an act!

09:34.220 --> 09:37.500
In other words, you were afraid those
 around you and the police would see that

09:37.500 --> 09:39.850
you were happy about your wife's 
death and thus had a motive,

09:40.160 --> 09:42.220
so you had no other choice!

09:42.220 --> 09:44.930
Because you're the killer, you had 
to try harder than anyone should

09:44.930 --> 09:48.290
to act like a grieving husband 
who had just lost his wife,

09:48.290 --> 09:50.060
so that no one would catch on!

09:51.960 --> 09:53.320
I see.

09:53.610 --> 09:55.060
Now I get it.

09:56.050 --> 09:59.450
You must've brought that girl here.

10:00.380 --> 10:04.420
You wanted to find a surprising 
way to declare that I killed Yukie,

10:04.420 --> 10:07.960
make me anxious, 
and psychologically corner me.

10:11.350 --> 10:12.210
No.

10:12.540 --> 10:14.960
She's a customer who has nothing 
to do with any of this.

10:15.330 --> 10:19.630
Besides, you only invited me 
out to lunch about an hour ago.

10:19.630 --> 10:23.350
Aw... That means the girl remains a mystery.

10:23.350 --> 10:26.550
How unfortunate. I wanted that cleared up.

10:27.100 --> 10:29.130
It is a fact that after I saw her,

10:29.130 --> 10:34.870
I thought of Kokuzo Bosatsu, a criminal 
trying to escape their crime, and seppuku.

10:35.320 --> 10:40.390
So her being here made me feel like the 
suspicions I've had for a while were true.

10:40.710 --> 10:44.390
It seemed like a revelation 
telling me to prosecute you...

10:46.110 --> 10:49.120
But I was completely wrong. 
This was my mistake.

10:49.510 --> 10:50.630
I'm sorry!

10:50.910 --> 10:52.570
You are not the murderer.

10:54.340 --> 10:55.990
What brought this on?

10:56.330 --> 10:59.550
It's not like you just told me something 
you randomly thought up yesterday.

10:59.900 --> 11:03.160
Besides, your analysis of my 
temperament is mostly right...

11:03.550 --> 11:05.790
It's <i>because</i> my analysis is correct.

11:05.790 --> 11:07.470
If you were indeed the murderer,

11:07.470 --> 11:09.740
there's no way you'd just keep

11:09.740 --> 11:13.400
happily eating your meal unfazed 
after I suddenly made that accusation.

11:13.660 --> 11:16.530
You'd have no time to worry about that girl.

11:16.760 --> 11:22.280
You'd get your brain working to try to assess 
the situation and how to deal with me.

11:22.520 --> 11:26.180
Then I could've been more 
certain about my hypothesis.

11:26.180 --> 11:30.220
And yet, you just seemed amused by the 
whole thing without a care in the world.

11:30.220 --> 11:33.540
You just kept wondering about 
that girl... That's inconceivable.

11:33.930 --> 11:37.550
To be honest, the way you seemed 
worn down seemed so natural,

11:38.050 --> 11:40.550
it was hard to determine 
if it was an act or not.

11:40.980 --> 11:42.610
I knew if I suddenly made that accusation,

11:42.610 --> 11:45.580
the mask of falsehood would fall off, but...

11:48.170 --> 11:52.230
I guess you really were run down 
because you lost Yukie-san.

11:52.530 --> 11:54.970
That would mean you're not the murderer.

11:57.480 --> 11:58.980
Who knows?

11:59.450 --> 12:05.070
To be honest, I didn't think Yukie's death 
would affect my health this much.

12:06.360 --> 12:10.190
I'll pay for everything here. 
It's the least I can do.

12:10.190 --> 12:11.750
Nah, don't worry about it.

12:12.260 --> 12:16.000
By the way, why didn't you take 
your suspicions to the police?

12:16.260 --> 12:19.000
Like I could ever sell my 
friend out to the police.

12:19.350 --> 12:23.350
I wouldn't be satisfied if I didn't at 
least give you the chance to confess.

12:23.350 --> 12:24.510
I see.

12:24.820 --> 12:27.560
Which means I should be the 
one to pay for everything here,

12:27.560 --> 12:30.520
like I said when I invited you out, Jujoji.

12:32.350 --> 12:34.110
You're a great friend.

12:34.110 --> 12:35.750
Thank you for the meal.

12:40.660 --> 12:42.280
Thank you very much.

12:54.780 --> 12:57.250
<i>What was her deal?</i>

13:03.280 --> 13:07.970
<b>A Lucky Day at the Unagi Restaurant</b>

13:07.970 --> 13:10.650
Hey, be careful getting home.

13:10.650 --> 13:11.720
Yeah...

13:11.720 --> 13:14.590
It'll be my treat next time.

13:18.490 --> 13:19.990
Do you have a moment,

13:20.300 --> 13:21.610
Kajio Takaya-san?

13:22.700 --> 13:23.380
Oh.

13:24.060 --> 13:25.950
Kokuzo Bosatsu.

13:27.050 --> 13:28.760
How do you know my name?

13:29.160 --> 13:31.740
I guess it'd be rude of me 
not to tell you my name.

13:32.630 --> 13:34.250
My name is Iwanaga Kotoko.

13:34.490 --> 13:40.000
I received a request regarding you, 
so could I have some of your time?

13:40.000 --> 13:42.370
Sure, what is it?

13:42.370 --> 13:45.860
Are you on your way to the 
police to turn yourself in?

13:47.110 --> 13:50.100
You regret purposely killing your wife,

13:50.390 --> 13:52.640
and you're thinking of turning 
yourself in, aren't you?

13:54.790 --> 13:57.520
<i>Jujoji's deduction was correct.</i>

13:57.970 --> 14:02.900
<i>Six months ago, I decided that I would 
murder Yukie so no one else could have her.</i>

14:03.280 --> 14:07.280
<i>I figured I could continue living my 
normal life, even after I killed Yukie.</i>

14:07.760 --> 14:10.530
<i>That's just the kind of person I am.</i>

14:11.050 --> 14:15.880
<i>To help conceal my true motive, 
I committed a number of muggings prior,</i>

14:15.880 --> 14:18.370
<i>and I made it look like I was a serial mugger</i>

14:18.370 --> 14:21.290
<i>who accidentally went too 
far and killed Yukie.</i>

14:23.470 --> 14:28.530
<i>Yukie died, and the police suspected nothing. 
Everything went according to plan.</i>

14:29.210 --> 14:31.800
<i>The one thing I didn't see coming was...</i>

14:32.120 --> 14:37.570
<i>After Yukie's funeral, my body became 
extremely heavy, and I was unable to sleep.</i>

14:40.900 --> 14:45.740
<i>I thought I'd be satisfied if I killed 
my wife, but that was overconfidence.</i>

14:46.260 --> 14:52.440
<i>Killing someone I loved must've tormented 
me far more than I could've imagined.</i>

14:52.860 --> 14:56.400
<i>Did I actually wish deep 
down for Yukie to live,</i>

14:56.400 --> 14:58.830
<i>even if she ended up with someone else?</i>

14:58.830 --> 15:00.940
I need to pay for my crimes...

15:01.700 --> 15:04.020
<i>I decided to turn myself in.</i>

15:04.460 --> 15:09.590
<i>After I had gotten everything 
in order, my body felt relieved.</i>

15:09.590 --> 15:11.450
<b>Unagi</b>

15:09.590 --> 15:11.450
<b>Unagi</b>

15:10.030 --> 15:13.090
<i>I wanted to eat something 
delicious on my last day,</i>

15:13.090 --> 15:15.350
<i>and I wanted to see my good friend.</i>

15:13.090 --> 15:15.350
This sake is great!

15:15.350 --> 15:20.600
<i>Before Jujoji even came up with deduction, 
I had decided I'd turn myself in.</i>

15:21.070 --> 15:24.610
<i>But this was the last place I thought 
he'd accuse me of killing Yukie.</i>

15:21.260 --> 15:24.610
I know I've suspected you this whole time...

15:24.610 --> 15:28.600
but will you continue being my friend?

15:25.340 --> 15:28.610
<i>Should I at least tell Jujoji? No...</i>

15:28.610 --> 15:31.060
<i>Right now, I want to part with a smile.</i>

15:29.950 --> 15:31.060
Of course.

15:31.380 --> 15:35.120
<i>It'd be way more fun to surprise him later.</i>

15:31.750 --> 15:34.170
Kajio! You bastard!

15:35.570 --> 15:39.560
<i>I was going to turn myself in 
today and end this whole thing.</i>

15:39.560 --> 15:42.870
<i>So how in the world does this 
girl know about this truth?</i>

15:44.360 --> 15:46.750
I see! This solves everything!

15:47.980 --> 15:51.170
You must be a detective 
or private investigator.

15:51.550 --> 15:54.680
I bet my wife's relatives asked you 
to investigate my surroundings,

15:54.900 --> 15:58.180
and you planted a wiretap in my 
apartment and found out what happened.

15:58.680 --> 16:02.950
It seems quite unreasonable 
for you to do a job like that,

16:02.950 --> 16:04.940
but I guess you're not as young as you look.

16:05.230 --> 16:09.130
What you were doing at that
unagi shop finally makes sense now.

16:09.130 --> 16:13.450
You must've been keeping an eye on me 
and preparing yourself to confront me.

16:13.950 --> 16:18.450
A girl like you alone at an authentic unagi 
shop would stand out like a sore thumb.

16:18.450 --> 16:20.270
And if said girl suddenly asked me

16:20.270 --> 16:24.460
about my crimes, I'd obviously panic, 
and you'd have the upper hand.

16:24.460 --> 16:27.870
I guess the revelation he was talking 
about wasn't a complete mistake.

16:27.870 --> 16:28.960
You really are

16:29.230 --> 16:33.380
the Kokuzo Bosatsu holding the 
treasured sword of wisdom.

16:34.610 --> 16:37.470
Unfortunately, I have no 
connection with any bosatsu.

16:37.810 --> 16:40.840
And I entered the shop you 
were in by pure coincidence.

16:40.840 --> 16:42.930
Aw, really?

16:43.670 --> 16:48.920
However, while I was there eating unaju, 
your wife requested something from me.

16:50.490 --> 16:51.650
My wife?

16:52.650 --> 16:55.580
Kajio-san, ever since your wife died,

16:55.580 --> 16:59.660
your body's felt heavy and you 
haven't been sleeping well, right?

16:59.930 --> 17:01.470
Of course you haven't.

17:01.470 --> 17:04.890
Because the ghost of your 
wife, whom you murdered,

17:04.890 --> 17:08.070
is clinging to you as hard as she can.

17:08.540 --> 17:09.670
Ghost?

17:09.940 --> 17:11.810
You've never heard of it?

17:12.140 --> 17:14.420
Sleep paralysis or other 
afflictions caused by spirits?

17:14.940 --> 17:17.180
That's what's happening to you.

17:17.460 --> 17:22.430
What's going on with your body is not 
a mental issue caused by your guilt.

17:23.060 --> 17:25.940
You're being weighed down 
heavily by an outside force.

17:27.060 --> 17:28.940
When I entered that unagi shop,

17:28.940 --> 17:32.090
I saw someone possessed by a ghost 
overflowing with a desire for revenge,

17:32.090 --> 17:33.940
so I was a bit surprised.

17:34.260 --> 17:40.450
And then, the ghost of your wife came 
over to me and explained everything.

17:40.450 --> 17:44.310
Since she was possessing you every minute 
of the day after being killed by you,

17:44.310 --> 17:45.690
she knew how the murder happened,

17:45.690 --> 17:48.960
along with everything you 
had been up to lately.

17:49.220 --> 17:53.460
And apparently, she has no plans of 
leaving you even if you turn yourself in.

17:53.870 --> 17:55.590
So basically, Kajio-san,

17:55.960 --> 17:58.370
even if you turn yourself in and get 
back into society's good graces,

17:58.370 --> 18:00.360
your ailments aren't going to get better.

18:00.360 --> 18:02.510
Please continue living as you have been.

18:06.930 --> 18:10.860
Could you not bring up random things 
like ghosts and sleep paralysis?

18:11.120 --> 18:15.540
Since I decided to turn myself in, my body 
feels lighter, and I've been able to sleep.

18:15.540 --> 18:17.860
That's because my guilt has been relieved.

18:18.130 --> 18:20.120
That's only your imagination.

18:20.120 --> 18:23.990
You just felt that way because you 
thought your ailments would go away

18:24.310 --> 18:26.360
if you tried to atone for your crimes.

18:27.270 --> 18:28.870
See? Even now...

18:28.870 --> 18:31.030
Your body already feels heavy, doesn't it?

18:46.310 --> 18:49.020
Your wife asked me to tell you this.

18:49.640 --> 18:54.110
You're not a decent human being 
who'd feel sick from guilt.

18:54.740 --> 18:57.310
You killed your wife because your 
desire to control her was so high,

18:57.310 --> 18:59.890
yet you don't even have the 
heart to feel guilty about that.

18:59.890 --> 19:01.670
You're just a heartless person.

19:02.510 --> 19:04.220
Apparently, it angers your wife to no end

19:04.220 --> 19:07.220
that you could possibly think 
yourself a decent human being

19:07.220 --> 19:10.290
who's able to feel guilty about anything.

19:10.700 --> 19:12.860
The sense of guilt you thought you felt

19:12.860 --> 19:14.790
was just a lie you fooled yourself with

19:15.230 --> 19:18.660
to justify how much you were suffering.

19:19.000 --> 19:21.050
You're truly just imagining things.

19:21.530 --> 19:23.070
You can go turn yourself in,

19:23.070 --> 19:25.430
or continue living out in 
the open as you have been.

19:25.820 --> 19:29.680
You'd lose your freedom living in prison, 
but you'd have clothes and food.

19:29.680 --> 19:32.100
You'd have your freedom if 
you lived out in the open,

19:30.570 --> 19:34.120
<i>This... This can't be happening...</i>

19:32.100 --> 19:35.660
but you'd have to continue trying to make 
a living with your current condition.

19:36.650 --> 19:38.410
I wonder which would be easier for you.

19:40.980 --> 19:42.920
W-Wait!

19:43.230 --> 19:46.590
You can see and hear ghosts, right?

19:46.590 --> 19:49.870
So if my wife's possessing me, 
you can exorcise her, can't you?!

19:49.870 --> 19:53.820
Would you do that for me? I'll pay—

19:54.620 --> 19:59.590
I am the Goddess of Wisdom to bakemono, 
ayakashi, ghosts, and demons.

19:59.810 --> 20:02.580
Even though I can honor your wife's 
request because she's a ghost,

20:02.580 --> 20:05.000
I have no obligation to honor 
the requests of humans.

20:05.430 --> 20:10.770
If your wife's possession of you went against 
the logic of this world, it'd be one thing,

20:10.770 --> 20:14.350
but this is retribution 
and makes complete sense.

20:14.570 --> 20:16.770
So there's no necessity 
for me to do anything.

20:16.770 --> 20:20.490
I'm sure your wife will grow bored
with possessing you someday.

20:20.940 --> 20:23.240
You'll just have to continue 
living until then.

20:23.480 --> 20:28.000
Not to mention, you get to stay with the 
wife you loved so much that you killed her.

20:28.000 --> 20:29.620
Isn't that what you wanted?

20:30.070 --> 20:32.070
<i>Who is this girl?</i>

20:32.610 --> 20:35.820
<i>If I just knock her down like I did Yukie...</i>

20:37.130 --> 20:38.650
<i>She's just a tiny girl.</i>

20:39.500 --> 20:41.130
<i>It'd be so easy...</i>

20:43.400 --> 20:44.660
Bosatsu...

20:44.660 --> 20:46.390
Again, you've got the wrong person.

20:46.860 --> 20:50.390
Could you... Could you just 
tell me one last thing?

20:50.690 --> 20:54.270
Why were you at that unagi shop all alone?

20:54.270 --> 20:57.130
I just can't figure it out.

20:57.130 --> 20:58.540
Why? Well...

20:58.990 --> 21:01.140
I'm spending the night at my 
boyfriend's place tonight,

21:01.140 --> 21:03.800
so I figured I'd need all 
the virility I could get.

21:04.260 --> 21:06.910
So I just entered the first 
unagi shop I saw. That's all.

21:08.710 --> 21:12.040
Unagi are known to symbolize healthy 
pregnancies and easy labor.

21:12.040 --> 21:14.460
And because they look like male genitalia,

21:14.460 --> 21:17.000
they also symbolize harmony 
among married couples.

21:17.000 --> 21:19.500
<i>The sheltered rich girl...</i>

21:19.790 --> 21:21.750
I must say, I do feel quite invigorated now.

21:22.300 --> 21:24.260
<i>The avatar of the Bosatsu...</i>

21:24.510 --> 21:26.260
I'm going to give it my all tonight!

21:26.480 --> 21:29.010
<i>She's so crass!</i>

21:29.330 --> 21:31.340
Well, enjoy the rest of your life!

21:35.930 --> 21:37.640
<i>Harmony among married couples...</i>

21:39.670 --> 21:40.680
Yukie...

21:44.040 --> 21:46.950
<i>Was I that heartless?</i>

21:48.030 --> 21:50.520
Good work, Kuro-kun.

21:48.030 --> 21:52.040
<b>Toraneko Delivery Service</b>

21:50.520 --> 21:52.040
You, too.

21:52.040 --> 21:54.010
Looks like someone's here to pick you up,

21:52.040 --> 21:55.790
Delivery Reception

21:54.010 --> 21:55.790
so you can clock out after you set that down.

21:55.790 --> 21:57.220
Pick me up?

21:57.220 --> 21:58.350
Senpai.

22:01.310 --> 22:02.800
Great job today.

22:02.800 --> 22:05.800
<b>Supermarket</b>

22:03.720 --> 22:05.800
So that happened.

22:05.800 --> 22:08.050
<b>Cheap</b>

22:05.800 --> 22:08.050
Thinly-sliced Beef Roast

22:05.800 --> 22:12.060
This Kajio guy definitely deserved what 
he got, but you sure are ruthless.

22:12.290 --> 22:16.390
I just did my job as the Goddess 
of Wisdom to the bakemono.

22:16.660 --> 22:19.070
Yeah, I know all that, so that's whatever.

22:19.070 --> 22:23.150
But from now on, don't go to any 
unagi shops on your own like that.

22:23.690 --> 22:24.670
<b>Fruit Balls</b>

22:23.880 --> 22:27.060
The owner was probably troubled 
by you being there, too.

22:27.400 --> 22:30.070
I fail to see the problem here...

22:28.340 --> 22:29.260
<b>Potato Chips
So good you can't stop!
Lightly salted</b>

22:30.920 --> 22:34.160
Perhaps I should've had a soft-shelled 
turtle dish instead, then?

22:34.400 --> 22:36.540
For the love of all things 
holy, don't do that, either.

22:36.920 --> 22:38.160
Seriously, just stop.

22:38.900 --> 22:42.580
Are you jealous that I had such 
expensive unagi all to myself?

22:41.170 --> 22:44.170
<b>Closed</b>

22:43.050 --> 22:46.030
But you had work during the day,

22:46.030 --> 22:48.300
so you wouldn't have been able 
to come even if I invited you.

22:49.830 --> 22:53.420
Okay, why don't I treat you next time?

22:53.420 --> 22:55.560
That's really not the point here.

22:55.900 --> 22:58.810
You work far too much anyway, Senpai.

22:59.220 --> 23:01.690
We don't even have time for dates.

23:02.220 --> 23:05.440
What kind of student works three 
or four heavy physical labor jobs

23:05.660 --> 23:08.410
without any sleep or days off?

23:09.450 --> 23:14.300
Good grief. It's so much trouble having 
a boyfriend who makes no sense.

23:14.680 --> 23:16.280
<i>Like you're one to talk...</i>

23:16.280 --> 23:20.960
Anyway, I ate unagi, so we 
must test out its potency!

23:21.480 --> 23:24.250
You don't need to hold back 
on me tonight, Senpai!

23:25.960 --> 23:29.970
<b>The End</b>
